## Minimal reproducible example

Below is a **complete, minimal HTML page** that shows a working custom style against a hosted vector tile source (replace the placeholders with your provider’s values). If this page renders correctly, you know the wiring is right; you can then copy the same source definition into your own project and focus on the layer definitions.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – custom style wiring demo</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>#map {position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;width:100%;}</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        // 👉 1️⃣ Use the provider’s TileJSON endpoint
        basemap: {
          type: 'vector',
          url: 'https://tiles.example.com/tileset.json',   // <-- replace
          // optional: promoteId if you need feature‑state later
          // promoteId: { roads: 'osm_id' }
        }
      },
      // 👉 2️⃣ Pull a tiny subset of the provider’s layers (you can add more)
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'water',
          type: 'fill',
          source: 'basemap',
          'source-layer': 'water',          // exact name from vector_layers
          paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' }
        },
        {
          id: 'roads',
          type: 'line',
          source: 'basemap',
          'source-layer': 'transportation',
          paint: {
            'line-color': '#ffffff',
            'line-width': 1
          }
        }
      ],
      // 👉 3️⃣ Glyphs & sprite (copy from provider’s style if you want labels/icons)
      glyphs: 'https://tiles.example.com/fonts/{fontstack}/{range}.pbf',
      sprite: 'https://tiles.example.com/sprites/basic'
    },
    center: [-122.447303, 37.753574],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // 👉 4️⃣ Insert a custom layer *below* the first label layer
  map.on('load', () => {
    const firstSymbol = map.getStyle().layers.find(l => l.type === 'symbol').id;
    const myPolygon = {
      id: 'my-polygon',
      type: 'fill',
      source: 'basemap',
      'source-layer': 'landuse',
      paint: { 'fill-color': '#ffcc00', 'fill-opacity': 0.4 }
    };
    map.addLayer(myPolygon, firstSymbol);
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**If this page works** but your own style still shows nothing, the problem is almost certainly in one of the following:

* A typo in `"source-layer"` (compare against the `vector_layers` list).  
* Adding your layers **after** the provider’s label layers (use the `firstSymbol` trick).  
* Forgetting to include `glyphs`/`sprite` when you need text or icons.  
* Using a `tiles` array without `minzoom`/`maxzoom` (causing empty tiles at the zoom you’re viewing).  

