## Quick “diagnostic” checklist you can run in the browser console

```js
// 1. Is the source present?
map.getSource('osm-raster');   // should return an object

// 2. Does the layer exist and reference the source?
map.getLayer('osm-basemap');   // should return an object with .source === 'osm-raster'

// 3. Are tiles being requested?
// Open DevTools → Network → filter “tile.openstreetmap.org” – you should see GETs for …/z/x/y.png

// 4. Are the requests succeeding (200) and not blocked by CORS?
// Look at the response headers for `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`

// 5. Is the raster layer below symbols?
const firstSymbol = map.getStyle().layers.find(l => l.type === 'symbol')?.id;
if (firstSymbol) {
  const rasterIdx = map.getStyle().layers.findIndex(l => l.id === 'osm-basemap');
  const symbolIdx = map.getStyle().layers.findIndex(l => l.id === firstSymbol);
  console.log('raster index', rasterIdx, 'symbol index', symbolIdx);
}
```

If any of those checks fail, adjust the corresponding piece of the style/source as described above.

